{
  "id": "L48",
  "subnivel": "A2.2",
  "unidad": 12,
  "titulo": "¿Alguna vez…?",
  "explicacion": [
    {
      "tipo": "texto",
      "md": "El **presente perfecto** habla de experiencias de tu vida, sin decir cuándo pasaron. Se forma con **have / has** + el **participio** del verbo."
    },
    {
      "tipo": "tabla",
      "filas": [
        [
          "I / You / We / They",
          "have + participio",
          "I have visited Canada."
        ],
        [
          "He / She / It",
          "has + participio",
          "She has visited Canada."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "tipo": "texto",
      "md": "Con **ever** (alguna vez) se pregunta y con **never** (nunca) se niega:"
    },
    {
      "tipo": "tabla",
      "filas": [
        [
          "Have you ever been to Canada?",
          "¿Has estado alguna vez en Canadá?"
        ],
        [
          "Yes, I have. / No, I haven't.",
          "Sí. / No."
        ],
        [
          "I have never been to Canada.",
          "Nunca he estado en Canadá."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "tipo": "tip",
      "md": "Al hablar, have y has se contraen: **I've** (I have), **she's** (she has), **haven't**, **hasn't**."
    },
    {
      "tipo": "texto",
      "md": "En los verbos regulares el participio es igual al pasado: visited, lived, tried. Los irregulares tienen su propia forma:"
    },
    {
      "tipo": "tabla",
      "columnas": [
        "Verbo",
        "Pasado",
        "Participio"
      ],
      "filas": [
        [
          "be",
          "was / were",
          "been"
        ],
        [
          "see",
          "saw",
          "seen"
        ],
        [
          "eat",
          "ate",
          "eaten"
        ],
        [
          "do",
          "did",
          "done"
        ],
        [
          "fly",
          "flew",
          "flown"
        ],
        [
          "write",
          "wrote",
          "written"
        ],
        [
          "ride",
          "rode",
          "ridden"
        ],
        [
          "meet",
          "met",
          "met"
        ],
        [
          "lose",
          "lost",
          "lost"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "tipo": "tip",
      "md": "Si dices **cuándo** pasó, usa pasado simple: *I went to Cancún in 2020*, no *I have been to Cancún in 2020*."
    },
    {
      "tipo": "texto",
      "md": "Experiencias:"
    },
    {
      "tipo": "tabla",
      "columnas": [
        "Inglés",
        "Español"
      ],
      "filas": [
        [
          "experience",
          "experiencia"
        ],
        [
          "abroad",
          "en el extranjero"
        ],
        [
          "try",
          "probar"
        ],
        [
          "ride a horse",
          "montar a caballo"
        ],
        [
          "climb a mountain",
          "escalar una montaña"
        ],
        [
          "concert",
          "concierto"
        ]
      ]
    }
  ],
